instrument wingie
; grain — voice and pearls: sing or talk into the Wingie.
; The left LED is the microphones, the right one what the scene makes.

a choir boy grown up overnight
------------------------------
; PSOLA: keys1 moves the pitch of your voice and keeps its vowels; fader1
; (Mix) moves the formants on purpose; the left LED follows the pitch it hears
the voice is psola samplerate=half   ; one voice: two PSOLAs are more than the Wingie has
mic.both -> voice
keys1.pitch -> voice.pitch
fader1 -40> voice.formant
voice -> out
voice.period -> lights.left
voice -> lights.right

a broken string of pearls
-------------------------
; Wishart's wavesets: each tap of mode1 is the clock for the stutters below;
; fader1 how many times a waveset repeats, fader2 the stutters' slices,
; fader3 their length
the pearls is wavesets repeat
the hand is beatgrains 3 burst=2 pattern=fifths samplerate=half
mic.both -> pearls hand
fader1 -> pearls.amount
mode1.tap -> hand.clock
fader2 -> hand.slices
fader3 -> hand.length
keys1.pitch -> hand.pitch
pearls hand -> left
pearls hand.right -> right
mic.both -> lights.left
hand -> lights.right

a hand on the reel
------------------
; hold mode1 to record (at least 0.15 s), then fader1 is the tape head:
; move it slowly to stretch, fast to sing, stop to hold; fader2 smooths the hand
the reel is scrub 6
mic.both -> reel
mode1 -> reel.record
fader1 -> reel.position
fader2 -> reel.smooth
reel -> out
mic.both -> lights.left
reel -> lights.right
